/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  NF270 INTRINSIC REJECTION OF NaCl AGAINST THE PERMEATE FLUX -- a dataset
  a membrane fit reads (fitParameters, residual kind membrane).

  Fernandez de Labastida & Yaroshchuk, Membranes 11 (2021) 272,
  doi:10.3390/membranes11040272 (CC BY 4.0), Figure 1a: the measured
  symbols, NaCl 0.01 mol/L, 20 C, flat NF270 in a rotating-disk cell, CP-
  corrected by the authors.  Digitised by bin/curate/digitise_fdl2021.py;
  written in this grammar by bin/curate/export_fdl2021_rejections.py
  (R = 1 - 1/f, Jv = J_v[um/s] x 1e-6).

  READING ERROR (not a measurement uncertainty -- none is published):
    J_v   8.239 um/s +- 0.06   f 1.7579 +- 0.0168
    J_v  12.344 um/s +- 0.06   f 2.1449 +- 0.0168
    J_v  20.153 um/s +- 0.06   f 3.7262 +- 0.0168
    J_v  27.732 um/s +- 0.06   f 4.8701 +- 0.0168
    J_v  36.172 um/s +- 0.06   f 5.9804 +- 0.0168
    J_v    45.1 um/s +- 0.06   f 7.0486 +- 0.0168
    J_v  55.837 um/s +- 0.06   f 6.2748 +- 0.0168

  NOT IN THE FEED BELOW: the 2e-4 mol/L NaNO3 + NH4Cl traces the authors
  added (2 % of the dominant salt).  The role this dataset plays -- fit or
  held out -- is declared by the operation that reads it, never here.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     membrane.rejection;
membrane     NF270;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus digitisedFromFigure;
    citation     "M. Fernandez de Labastida, A. Yaroshchuk, Nanofiltration of Multi-Ion Solutions: Quantitative Control of Concentration Polarization and Interpretation by Solution-Diffusion-Electro-Migration Model, Membranes 11 (2021) 272, Figure 1a";
    identity     "one series of the study cited above; no doi identity: the four fdl2021_* datasets are four salts of ONE study, and a held-out one is held out WITHIN that study, not an independent study";
    licence      CC-BY-4.0;
}

T            293.15 K;
feed         { NaCl 10 mol/m3; }

columns
(
    { name Jv;  unit m/s; }
    { name R_NaCl;  unit -; }
);

data
(
    8.239000e-06  0.431139
    1.234400e-05  0.533778
    2.015300e-05  0.731630
    2.773200e-05  0.794665
    3.617200e-05  0.832787
    4.510000e-05  0.858128
    5.583700e-05  0.840632
);
